\paragraph{Practitioner guidelines.}
Monitor for CIVO using the NVE diagnostic ($\geq 1.5\times$, AUROC${=}0.953$, in-sample, post-hoc; Appendix~\ref{sec:roc_analysis}). Wide dual-critic offers the highest prevention rate (3/4, Walker only) but does not transfer cross-environment. Avoid gradient-level interventions (compensatory amplification) and output-level value capping (anchor pollution).

\paragraph{Implications for robot learning.}
CIVO poses heightened risk in robotics, where value overestimation can drive policies toward dangerous actions on real hardware. As DreamerV3-family methods see increasing deployment on physical robots \citep{wu2023daydreamer}, CIVO may arise whenever practitioners introduce $\dt$-conditioning for multi-rate control. Our NVE diagnostic provides a lightweight online monitor applicable to any Dreamer-based robot controller; the dual-critic mechanism offers practical prevention without hyperparameter tuning beyond capacity allocation. Our PickCube-v1 results (Table~\ref{tab:factorial_results}) confirm that CIVO generalizes beyond locomotion to manipulation tasks with sparse rewards, where the failure mode is particularly consequential.

