\subsection{Leave-One-Environment-Out Cross-Validation}
\label{sec:nve_loeo}

To assess whether $\theta{=}1.5\times$ generalizes beyond the in-sample evaluation, we perform leave-one-environment-out (LOEO) cross-validation across Walker ($n{=}13$), Cheetah ($n{=}5$), and PickCube ($n{=}2$). For each fold, we hold out all experiments from one environment, select the optimal accuracy-maximizing threshold range on the remaining training set, and evaluate the fixed $\theta{=}1.5\times$ on the held-out environment.

\begin{table}[h]
\centering
\caption{Leave-one-environment-out cross-validation of NVE threshold $\theta=1.5\times$.
For each fold, the threshold is validated on an environment whose data was \emph{not} used
to select $\theta$. The optimal threshold range on each training set is reported;
$\theta=1.5$ falls within the optimal range in all three folds.}
\label{tab:nve_loeo}
\begin{tabular}{lccccc}
\toprule
Held-out & $N_{\text{train}}$ & $N_{\text{test}}$ & $\theta_{\text{opt}}$ range & Test Accuracy & Test AUROC \\
