The threshold $\theta{=}1.5\times$ falls within the optimal accuracy range for all three training folds: $(1.45, 1.53]$ when Walker data is available, and the wider $(1.00, 3.78)$ when training on Cheetah$+$PickCube only (where CIVO and non-CIVO NVE values are well-separated). The single cross-validation error is exp\_008e\_v3 seed~2 (Walker), an IRD collapse mechanistically distinct from CIVO (\S\ref{sec:roc_analysis}). Mean held-out accuracy is 0.974 and mean AUROC is 0.981, confirming that $\theta{=}1.5\times$ generalizes across environments without retuning. PickCube fold confidence intervals remain wide (Clopper-Pearson 95\% CI: $[0.158, 1.000]$) due to $N_{\text{test}}{=}2$.

